# Titan Orbit — Netcode for Entities (standard practice)

Stack is **Netcode for Entities 6.6** (NCE / DOTS), **not** Netcode for GameObjects (NGO).
Docs: https://docs.unity3d.com/Packages/com.unity.netcode@6.6/manual/index.html

This project is a **dedicated server**: the server world is the only simulation authority. Clients gather input, predict ships that must collide, interpolate map bodies, and render. Do not add listen-server / host-authoritative / NGO patterns.

Paired: `titan-orbit-ship-simulation.mdc` (flight feel), `titan-orbit-headless-server-rebuild.mdc` (when to rebuild).

---

## 1. Worlds — tag every system

NCE runs isolated ECS worlds. A system with no filter is created in **both** client and server `SimulationSystemGroup`. Always declare the world.

| Flag | Use |
|------|-----|
| `WorldSystemFilterFlags.ServerSimulation` | Authoritative sim, validation, spawning, economy |
| `WorldSystemFilterFlags.ClientSimulation` | Input gather, prediction wiring, interpolation, presentation |
| Both (`Server \| Client`) | Shared predicted gameplay (same code, both worlds) |
| `ThinClientSimulation` | Only if the system must run on MPPM thin clients |

`[UpdateInGroup(typeof(GhostInputSystemGroup))]` already implies client. `PresentationSystemGroup` exists on clients only — never put render/audio/HUD in the server world.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — runs on dedicated server (no GPU / no local player)
public partial struct ShipVfxSystem : ISystem { }

// ✅ GOOD — client presentation only
[WorldSystemFilter(WorldSystemFilterFlags.ClientSimulation)]
[UpdateInGroup(typeof(PresentationSystemGroup))]
public partial struct ShipVfxSystem : ISystem { }

// ✅ GOOD — predicted gameplay, written once, runs on both
[WorldSystemFilter(WorldSystemFilterFlags.ServerSimulation | WorldSystemFilterFlags.ClientSimulation)]
[UpdateInGroup(typeof(PredictedSimulationSystemGroup))]
public partial struct ShipMotorSystem : ISystem { }
```

