## 2. Ghosts — replicate state, not events

Replicated entities are **ghosts**. Bake a `GhostAuthoringComponent` on the prefab. Mark replicated fields with `[GhostField]`. Use `GhostComponentVariation` / quantization when you need a smaller wire format without changing the gameplay type.

| Ghost | `GhostAuthoring` | Why |
|-------|------------------|-----|
| Player ships | `HasOwner`, `SupportAutoCommandTarget`, **Predicted** (`SupportedGhostModes = All`) | Local hull stays Predicted. Clients switch remotes via `GhostPredictionSwitchingQueues` (`ShipClientPredictionSwitchSystem`): nearest in ram range Predicted (same timeline), others Interpolated. Server remains two-body authority. Do not bake `OwnerPredicted` (cannot switch). |
| Map bodies (planets / asteroids / gems) | **Interpolated** | Snapshot pose only; ships do not two-body-push them this tick |
| Short-lived movers | Interpolated + **Dynamic** optimize | Pose must keep sending |

Do **not** predict every remote hull and do **not** add a custom interpolated-remote sweep. Official NCE path: predict the local ship plus ghosts it is colliding with (`ShipClientPredictionSwitchSystem` radius + cap); interpolate the rest. Predicted vs interpolated live on different timelines (~2× ping) — that mix feels choppy on ram. Server predicts every hull and owns two-body knockback. Predicting all remotes forced an 8-step catch-up spiral (`DefaultGhostMode` must not be `OwnerPredicted`).

Server sets `GhostOwner.NetworkId` to the owning `NetworkId`. Clients test ownership with `GhostOwnerIsLocal` (not a hand-rolled id check).

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — replicate derived / visual-only data every tick
[GhostField] public float3 MeshDisplayPosition;

// ✅ GOOD — replicate authoritative sim state; derive presentation on the client
[GhostField] public int Population;
[GhostField(Quantization = 1000)] public float CurrentGems;
```

Do not invent a second snapshot protocol. Do not send `LocalTransform` every frame as an RPC.

