## 3. Input and prediction

Tick-based prediction — not client-sent positions.

1. **Gather** (client only) in `GhostInputSystemGroup`. Write an `IInputComponentData` on the owned ghost (`GhostOwnerIsLocal`). Use `InputEvent` for one-shots (`GetKeyDown`).
2. **Process** (client + server, same code) in `PredictedSimulationSystemGroup`. Physics-coupled motors go in `PredictedFixedStepSimulationSystemGroup` (NCE moves `PhysicsSystemGroup` there).
3. Predicted queries include `.WithAll<PredictedGhost, Simulate>()`. `Simulate` is how NCE skips ghosts that already have a newer snapshot (partial snapshots).
4. Use `NetworkTime` / prediction `TimeData`. Never poll `UnityEngine.Input` inside the prediction loop. Server **must not** overwrite received commands.

```csharp
[UpdateInGroup(typeof(GhostInputSystemGroup))]
[WorldSystemFilter(WorldSystemFilterFlags.ClientSimulation)]
public partial struct GatherShipInputSystem : ISystem { /* write IInputComponentData */ }

[UpdateInGroup(typeof(PredictedFixedStepSimulationSystemGroup))]
[WorldSystemFilter(WorldSystemFilterFlags.ServerSimulation | WorldSystemFilterFlags.ClientSimulation)]
public partial struct DriveShipSystem : ISystem
{
    public void OnUpdate(ref SystemState state)
    {
        foreach (var (transform, input) in
                 SystemAPI.Query<RefRW<LocalTransform>, RefRO<ShipInput>>()
                     .WithAll<PredictedGhost, Simulate>())
        {
            // same motor math on client (predict) and server (authoritative)
        }
    }
}
```

In this repo: `ShipInput` (`IInputComponentData`), gather via `ShipInputApplySystem`, shared motor `ShipPhysicsDriveLogic`.

One-shot predicted VFX/spawns: gate with `NetworkTime.IsFirstTimeFullyPredictingTick` so rollback does not replay them.

---

## 4. RPCs — one-off, reliable, not state

Use `IRpcCommand` for join/team/chat/purchases/map-flow — not for per-tick pose or health.

- Client: create entity with the command + `SendRpcCommandRequest` (target is the server).
- Server: query `ReceiveRpcCommandRequest`, apply, **destroy** the request entity.
- Server → one client: set `SendRpcCommandRequest.TargetConnection`. `Entity.Null` broadcasts.
- RPCs are reliable and not tick-aligned. Late joiners will **not** see past RPCs — persistent facts belong on ghosts.

```csharp
// ❌ BAD — movement as an RPC
public struct SetShipPositionRpc : IRpcCommand { public float3 Position; }

// ✅ GOOD — one-off command; result lives on a ghost field
public struct RequestTeamCommand : IRpcCommand { public int TeamId; }
```

In this repo: `NetworkCommands.cs`.

---

## 5. Dedicated server and testing

- **Authority:** server simulates each tick once. Client prediction is a forecast; the server snapshot wins.
- **Headless:** `UNITY_SERVER` has no `PresentationSystemGroup`. Do not `#if !UNITY_SERVER` gameplay that the server must also run.
- **Tick rate:** `ClientServerTickRate` on the server (`SimulationTickRate`, `NetworkTickRate`). Do not drive predicted motors from `Time.deltaTime`.
- **Test:** Multiplayer Play Mode (MPPM) in Editor. Deployed GCE/Linux binaries only change after a dedicated server rebuild (see headless-rebuild rule).
- **Thin clients** are input-only soak tools — they are not a second gameplay architecture.

---

## Forbidden (leave the standard path)

- NGO `NetworkBehaviour` / `NetworkVariable` / client-authoritative transforms
- Custom UDP/WebSocket gameplay protocols alongside NCE ghosts
- GameObject `Rigidbody` / PhysX as a second predicted motor
- Client-only “corrections” that the server will not simulate (god-mode speed, fake hits)
- Systems that run predicted state **and** presentation without a world filter

---

## Agent checklist

- [ ] `WorldSystemFilter` (or a group that implies one) on every new system
- [ ] Continuous state → ghost `[GhostField]`; one-off → `IRpcCommand`
- [ ] Ships that collide: Predicted default + `SupportedGhostModes = All`; client switches remotes to Interpolated; `IInputComponentData` + `GhostOwnerIsLocal` for the owner (gather only)
- [ ] Map bodies: Interpolated; presentation reads interpolated pose. Predicted ships read predicted pose
- [ ] Predicted writes in `PredictedSimulationSystemGroup` / `PredictedFixedStep…`; gather in `GhostInputSystemGroup`
- [ ] Shared predicted logic is identical on client and server
- [ ] Predicted queries use `PredictedGhost` + `Simulate`
- [ ] No NGO APIs, no per-frame position RPCs, no server presentation systems
